  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When building a world in Unity, a standard climbing and swimming prefab would allow for players to mark certain objects as climbable and certain areas as swimmable.\n\nSuggesting this because I'm noticing more and more casual worlds implementing climbing prefabs and using them for water too.\n\nFor swimming, the suggested mod could include checkboxes that state if players are automatically buoyant and would need to manually swim down. If not, they would sink slowly into the water, according to whatever gravity mod the player sets for that area.",
